COMMENT ON TABLE operations.emergency IS E'Layer 2 operational state. An unresolved Emergency is NEVER an infinite Resource reservation. Runtime guards make declaration start at database NOW, keep the declared cascade range canonical [declared_at, expected_end_at), require the expected end inside the declaration Operating Session, serialize Venue/Resource races, enforce the canonical status transition graph, and couple ACTIVE/AWAITING versus ENDED/CONVERTED atomically to the matching Operational Selling Block. ended_at is the physical resolution timestamp for ENDED or CONVERTED.\n\nSource/critical constraints include scope, status, scope shape, conversion target/shape, time order, canonical declared period and lifecycle shape.';
